---
import WindowPage from '../layouts/WindowPage.astro';
import PolicyLinks from '../components/PolicyLinks.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';

/* Community guidelines (D35): the house rules for comments (D37), likes and screen names. */
const mail = `mailto:${SITE.email}`;
---

<WindowPage
  title="Community guidelines"
  windowTitle="Guidelines - Internet Grails"
  description={`The house rules for comments, likes and profiles on ${SITE.name}.`}
  backHref="/about/"
>
  <h1>Community guidelines</h1>
  <p>
    These are the house rules for comments, likes and screen names on {SITE.name}. The aim is a
    comment section that feels like the best group chat you were ever in: funny, a bit chaotic,
    never cruel.
  </p>

  <h2>Do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Be funny, be weird, argue about the meme. Roast the post, not the person.</li>
    <li>Credit people. If you know who made something, say so.</li>
    <li>Report anything that breaks these rules instead of replying to it.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Don't</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Harass or threaten anyone</strong>, or pile on someone, including the people in the
      memes.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Post hate</strong> aimed at people for their race, ethnicity, religion, gender,
      sexuality, disability or similar.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Share anyone's private information</strong>: addresses, phone numbers, private photos,
      screenshots of private messages.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Post sexual content involving minors</strong>, ever. We report it to the authorities.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Post graphic violence, porn, or anything illegal.</strong>
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Spam</strong>: ads, scams, link drops, or posting the same thing over and over.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Pretend to be someone you're not</strong>, including {SITE.name} or the people who run
      it.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Post other people's work as your own.</strong>
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What happens if you break them</h2>
  <p>
    Use <strong>Report</strong> on a comment to flag it. A person reviews what gets reported, and a
    comment several members report is hidden until they do. Depending on how bad it is, we may hide
    the comment or ban you from commenting. If you think we got it wrong, email{' '}
    <a href={mail}>{SITE.email}</a>.
  </p>

  <PolicyLinks />
</WindowPage>
